# ProConnectiv Project Rules

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: React 18, Vite 7, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui (New York), Wouter, TanStack React Query
- Backend: Express 5, PostgreSQL, Drizzle ORM, Firebase Admin
- Real-time: WebSocket (ws) for WebRTC signaling
- Language: TypeScript (strict mode)

## Path Aliases
- `@/*` → `client/src/*`
- `@shared/*` → `shared/*`
- `@assets` → `attached_assets`

## Code Conventions
- Use Drizzle ORM for all database queries (schema in `shared/schema.ts`)
- Validate API inputs with Zod schemas
- Use shadcn/ui components from `client/src/components/ui/`
- Use TanStack React Query for all data fetching
- Server routes are registered in `server/routes.ts`
- Admin: `users.role = 'admin'` in Postgres; first admin via `POST /api/admin/register` + `ADMIN_REGISTER_SECRET` (or SQL); not linked from public UI; admins use `PATCH /api/admin/users/:userId/role` and `GET /api/admin/connection-requests`

## Available Agent Tools
- **Agency agents**: Use `@frontend-developer`, `@backend-architect`, `@security-engineer`, etc. for specialized reviews
- **Impeccable skills**: Use `/audit`, `/polish`, `/normalize`, `/critique` for UI design reviews
- **PromptFoo**: Run `npm run test:prompts` to test AI prompts
- **Recall AI**: `server/recall-ai.ts` provides meeting bot integration (needs RECALL_API_KEY)
- **OpenViking**: Context database in `.viking/` for agent memory
